Extensions in auto-discovered locations can be hot-reloaded with `/reload`\n33\t\n34\t### Hook Names and Protocol Mapping\n35\t| Native Event Name | When It Fires | Protocol Event Type | Verified |\n36\t|------------------|---------------|---------------------|----------|\n37\t| `session_start` | Initial session load | 1 = SessionStart | Yes |\n38\t| `before_agent_start` | After user submits prompt, before agent loop | 2 = TurnStart | Yes |\n39\t| `turn_end` | Each LLM turn completes (tool use or final) | (internal, not a lifecycle event) | Yes |\n40\t| `agent_end` | Agent loop ends (all turns complete) | 3 = TurnEnd | Yes |\n41\t| `session_shutdown` | Process exit (Ctrl+C, Ctrl+D, or -p mode exit) | (cleanup only) | Yes |\n42\t\n43\t### Hook Input Format (Extension → Binary)\n44\tThe TypeScript extension constructs JSON and passes it to `entire agent hook pi <event>` on stdin:\n45\t\n46\t**session_start** (verified):\n47\t```json\n48\t{\n49\t  \"type\": \"session_start\",\n50\t  \"cwd\": \"/path/to/repo\",\n51\t  \"session_file\": \"/Users/.../.pi/agent/sessions/<encoded-path>/<timestamp>_<uuid>.jsonl\"\n52\t}\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\t**before_agent_start** (verified):\n56\t```json\n57\t{\n58\t  \"type\": \"before_agent_start\",\n59\t  \"cwd\": \"/path/to/repo\",\n60\t  \"session_file\": \"/Users/.../.pi/agent/sessions/<encoded-path>/<timestamp>_<uuid>.jsonl\",\n61\t  \"prompt\": \"user prompt text\"\n62\t}\n63\t```\n64\t\n65\t**agent_end** (verified):\n66\t```json\n67\t{\n68\t  \"type\": \"agent_end\",\n69\t  \"cwd\": \"/path/to/repo\",\n70\t  \"session_file\": \"/Users/.../.pi/agent/sessions/<encoded-path>/<timestamp>_<uuid>.jsonl\",\n71\t  \"message_count\": 4\n72\t}\n73\t```\n74\t\n75\t**session_shutdown** (verified):\n76\t```json\n77\t{\n78\t  \"type\": \"session_shutdown\"\n79\t}\n80\t```\n81\t\n82\t## Session Management\n83\t- Session directory: `~/.pi/agent/sessions/<encoded-path>/`\n84\t  - `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` env var overrides `~/.pi/agent` base\n85\t- Path encoding: absolute path with `/` → `-`, wrapped in `--` prefix/suffix\n86\t  - Example: `/Users/nodo/work/repo` → `--Users-nodo-work-repo--` (verified)\n87\t- Session file pattern: `<ISO-timestamp>_<uuid>.jsonl`\n88\t  - Example: `2026-03-27T21-38-13-384Z_34567c89-98b3-4cc3-a76d-1a4a67193648.jsonl` (verified)\n89\t- Session ID source: UUID from the session file header entry (first line, `id` field) (verified)\n90\t- Session file format: JSONL (newline-delimited JSON, one entry per line)\n91\t- Resume mechanism: `pi --continue` (most recent) or `pi --session <path>` (specific file)\n92\t\n93\t## Transcript\n94\t- Location: `~/.pi/agent/sessions/<encoded-path>/<timestamp>_<uuid>.jsonl` (verified)\n95\t- Format: JSONL with tree structure (entries have `id` and `parentId`)\n96\t- Version: 3 (verified from session header)\n97\t\n98\t### Entry Types (verified)\n99\t| Entry Type | Fields | Purpose |\n100\t|-----------|--------|---------|\n101\t| `session` | `version`, `id`, `timestamp`, `cwd` | Session header (first line) |\n102\t| `model_change` | `provider`, `modelId` | Model selection |\n103\t| `thinking_level_change` | `thinkingLevel` | Thinking level setting |\n104\t| `message` | `message` object with `role`, `content`, etc. | All messages |\n105\t\n106\t### Message Roles (verified)\n107\t| Role | Content Types | Key Fields |\n108\t|------|--------------|------------|\n109\t| `user` | `text` | `content[].text` |\n110\t| `assistant` | `text`, `toolCall`, `thinking` | `content[]`, `usage`, `stopReason`, `model`, `provider` |\n111\t| `toolResult` | `text` | `toolCallId`, `toolName`, `content[]`, `isError` |\n112\t\n113\t### Tool Call Format (verified)\n114\t```json\n115\t{\n116\t  \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n117\t  \"id\": \"REDACTED\",\n118\t  \"name\": \"write\",\n119\t  \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"hello.txt\", \"content\": \"hello world\\n\"}\n120\t}\n121\t```\n122\t\n123\tFile-modifying tools:\n124\t- `write`: `arguments.path` (file path), `arguments.content` (file content)\n125\t- `edit`: `arguments.path` (file path), `arguments.oldText` / `arguments.newText` or `arguments.edits[]`\n126\t- `bash`: may modify files but path extraction is unreliable\n127\t\n128\t### Token Usage Format (verified)\n129\t```json\n130\t{\n131\t  \"input\": 2572,\n132\t  \"output\": 73,\n133\t  \"cacheRead\": 0,\n134\t  \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n135\t  \"totalTokens\": 2645,\n136\t  \"cost\": {\"input\": 0.01286, \"output\": 0.001825, \"cacheRead\": 0, \"cacheWrite\": 0, \"total\": 0.014685}\n137\t}\n138\t```\n139\t\n140\t## Data Storage Verification\n141\t- Session files contain actual assistant content: **YES** (verified — full response text, tool calls with arguments, thinking blocks)\n142\t- Secondary storage location: **none needed** — all data is in the JSONL session file\n143\t- Hook data flow verified: **YES** — extension receives event data, ctx provides session file path and cwd\n144\t- Verification method: Ran `pi -p` with a known prompt, inspected JSONL session file for actual tool call arguments and response text\n145\t\n146\t## Protocol Mapping\n147\t| Subcommand | Native Concept | Implementation Notes | Feasibility |\n148\t|-----------|---------------|---------------------|-------------|\n149\t| `info` | static metadata | Return name \"pi\", type \"Pi\", capabilities | Required |\n150\t| `detect` | `pi` binary | Check `command -v pi` or `.pi/` in repo | Required |\n151\t| `get-session-id` | session header UUID | Extract from hook input `session_file` path (UUID after `_`) or read first line of JSONL | Required |\n152\t| `get-session-dir` | `.entire/tmp` | Use default Entire session dir | Required |\n153\t| `resolve-session-file` | `.entire/tmp/<id>.json` | Standard path resolution | Required |\n154\t| `read-session` | JSONL transcript | Read Pi's JSONL, build AgentSession with native_data | Required |\n155\t| `write-session` | cached transcript | Write normalized session data to session ref | Required |\n156\t| `read-transcript` | JSONL file bytes | Read raw bytes from Pi session or cached `.entire/tmp/<id>.json` | Required |\n157\t| `chunk-transcript` | raw bytes | Base64 chunk by max size | Required |\n158\t| `reassemble-transcript` | base64 chunks | Reassemble chunks | Required |\n159\t| `compact-transcript` | compact JSONL | Emit normalized Entire compact transcript JSONL for checkpoints v2 | Compact transcript |\n160\t| `format-resume-command` | `pi --continue` | Return `pi --continue` or `pi --session <path>` | Required |\n161\t| `parse-hook` | extension event JSON | Map extension JSON to EventJSON (type 1/2/3) | Hooks |\n162\t| `install-hooks` | `.pi/extensions/entire/` | Write TypeScript extension that calls `entire agent hook pi <event>` | Hooks |\n163\t| `uninstall-hooks` | remove extension dir | Delete `.pi/extensions/entire/` | Hooks |\n164\t| `are-hooks-installed` | check extension exists | Check for `.pi/extensions/entire/index.ts` | Hooks |\n165\t| `get-transcript-position` | file size | Return byte count of transcript file | Transcript analyzer |\n166\t| `extract-modified-files` | tool call parsing | Extract `path` from `write` and `edit` tool calls in JSONL | Transcript analyzer |\n167\t| `extract-prompts` | user message parsing | Extract text from `role: \"user\"` messages | Transcript analyzer |\n168\t| `extract-summary` | last assistant text | Extract last `role: \"assistant\"` text content | Transcript analyzer |\n169\t\n170\t## Selected Capabilities\n171\t| Capability | Declared | Justification |\n172\t|-----------|----------|---------------|\n173\t| hooks | true | Pi has a TypeScript extension system with lifecycle events (verified) |\n174\t| transcript_analyzer | true | JSONL transcripts contain full structured data — tool calls, prompts, responses (verified) |\n175\t| transcript_preparer | false | JSONL files are directly readable, no pre-processing needed |\n176\t| token_calculator | true | Assistant messages contain `usage` with input/output/cache tokens (verified) |\n177\t| com